This is a miscompilation bug in VectorCombine.
Issue title: VectorCombine transform leading to srem by poison
Detailed information:
BUG TYPE:
    miscompilation

VERIFICATION RESULT:
    Invalid refinement in @shuf_srem_v4i32_poison -- Source is more defined than target

VIOLATED PROPERTY:
    UB refinement

SOURCE (pre-transformation IR):
target triple = "x86_64-unknown-unknown"
define <4 x i32> @shuf_srem_v4i32_poison(<4 x i32> %a0, <4 x i32> %a1) {
  %srem0 = srem <4 x i32> %a1, %a0
  %srem1 = srem <4 x i32> splat (i32 1), %a0
  %r = shufflevector <4 x i32> %srem0, <4 x i32> %srem1, <4 x i32> <i32 0, i32 poison, i32 6, i32 3>
  ret <4 x i32> %r
}

TARGET (post-transformation IR):
target triple = "x86_64-unknown-unknown"
define <4 x i32> @shuf_srem_v4i32_poison(<4 x i32> %a0, <4 x i32> %a1) #0 {
  %1 = shufflevector <4 x i32> %a1, <4 x i32> <i32 1, i32 1, i32 1, i32 1>, <4 x i32> <i32 0, i32 poison, i32 6, i32 3>
  %2 = shufflevector <4 x i32> %a0, <4 x i32> poison, <4 x i32> <i32 0, i32 poison, i32 2, i32 3>
  %r = srem <4 x i32> %1, %2
  ret <4 x i32> %r
}

WHAT THE TRANSFORMATION CHANGED:
  modified:
    %r
      source: %r = shufflevector <4 x i32> %srem0, <4 x i32> %srem1, <4 x i32> <i32 0, i32 poison, i32 6, i32 3>
      target: %r = srem <4 x i32> %1, %2
  only in target:
    %1: %1 = shufflevector <4 x i32> %a1, <4 x i32> <i32 1, i32 1, i32 1, i32 1>, <4 x i32> <i32 0, i32 poison, i32 6, i32 3>
    %2: %2 = shufflevector <4 x i32> %a0, <4 x i32> poison, <4 x i32> <i32 0, i32 poison, i32 2, i32 3>
  only in source:
    %srem0: %srem0 = srem <4 x i32> %a1, %a0
    %srem1: %srem1 = srem <4 x i32> splat (i32 1), %a0

CRITICAL VALUES:
    %r
    %srem0
    %srem1

DEPENDENCY CHAIN (source):
    %srem0 = srem <4 x i32> %a1, %a0
    %srem1 = srem <4 x i32> splat (i32 1), %a0
    %r = shufflevector <4 x i32> %srem0, <4 x i32> %srem1, <4 x i32> <i32 0, i32 poison, i32 6, i32 3>

CONTROL FLOW (blocks entered by the failing execution):
    (none)

COUNTEREXAMPLE INPUT:
    <4 x i32> %a0 = < #x00000001 (1), #x00000001 (1), #x00000001 (1), #x00000001 (1) >
    <4 x i32> %a1 = < #x00000000 (0), #x00000000 (0), #x00000000 (0), #x00000000 (0) >

DIVERGENCE (source vs target on that input):
    %r: source = < #x00000000 (0), poison, #x00000000 (0), #x00000000 (0) >   target = UB triggered!

INTERPRETATION:
    A transformation may not introduce undefined behaviour. Any execution that is UB-free in the source must remain UB-free in the target.
